Ezero file extension validation, 2026-11-17

Completed on the frozen own Zero compiler b9b807:
  Linux suite: 58/58 checks passed.
  Windows suite: 46/46 checks passed, native PE programs executed under Wine.
Each suite includes actual file/runtime execution and frontend arity/path
checks; the compile-only cases are not presented as runtime executions.
Frontend, packer and generated runtime are original Zero. Environmental test
orchestration is private external validation, not product source or a runtime
dependency. No claim of testing on physical Windows hardware is made.

Covered create/save/read/readfile/writefile/del/rm/watch/search/go/disks;
existing-file preservation; explicit save replacement; empty and Unicode text;
Unicode/spaced native paths; exact 65536-byte round trip and overflow rejection;
listing 2048/2049-item and byte limits; repeated listing collection with live
path and retained text roots; one-based results; exact/*/? case-sensitive
matching including accented and supplementary Unicode scalars; directory
refusal; malformed UTF-8 and embedded NUL; invalid types and arities; bare Zero
drive paths; and normal argument/list separator regression. Oversized save
text was rejected before modifying an existing private fixture. Linux also
checked final-symlink/FIFO refusal, invalid UTF-8 filenames and newline names.

The first Windows candidate failed listing tests. Isolated probes identified
incorrect stack displacements in the platform helper. The corrected compiler
and its final stack-bound fix were used to rebuild every final Windows PE
fixture. The entire suite then passed; failed preliminary runs are not counted.

Independent real Zero OS verification by the guest service agent passed the
compact files_guest.ezero sequence in BIOS32, BIOS64, UEFI32 and UEFI64. Each
mode also handled a missing-file Ezero runtime error followed by a successful
next program. The component's full VM fixture covered 40 terminal commands per
mode, including Zero operations and reboot persistence. Canonical full OS evidence is
verification/guest-files-0.12/report.ztext; native/Wine execution alone is not guest evidence.

External detail reports:
/tmp/zero-support/validation-0.12/ezero/linux-2bukgpum/results.txt
/tmp/zero-support/validation-0.12/ezero/windows-pbxmf9a7/results.txt

Passing finite checks is not proof of the absence of all defects. Native save
is explicit non-atomic replacement. The guest writable ZeroFS profile still
has eight slots, 31-byte ASCII names and 400 printable ASCII bytes per file.
Guest applications share kernel memory; this API does not add process isolation.

